package sift.override

import rego.v1

# Per-invocation operator overrides (G3). An override is a verifiable
# credential the operator signs; the proxy verifies it cryptographically and
# injects the verified claims as input.context.operator_override before
# evaluation. This package applies the OPERATOR CEILING: the hard bound on what
# any override is allowed to widen. Crypto lives in Go; only the ceiling logic
# lives here.
#
# operator_override.capabilities names the policy categories the override asks
# to waive. cleared_packages is the intersection of that request with the
# operator-configured ceiling (data.override_ceiling). A category outside the
# ceiling can NEVER be waived, no matter what a (validly signed) override asks
# for — so an over-broad or stolen override cannot widen past the operator's
# static intent. With the default empty ceiling, nothing is waivable.
cleared_packages contains pkg if {
	some pkg in input.context.operator_override.capabilities
	pkg in data.override_ceiling
}

# active reports that a verified override accompanied this call (it carries an
# issuer). Drives audit provenance; not part of the allow decision itself.
active if input.context.operator_override.iss
